2
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Steven Universe: The Movie is a tv movie, adventure,
animation film directed by Rebecca Sugar.

3
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Two years after bringing peace to the galaxy, Steven Universe sees his past come back to
haunt him in the form of a deranged Gem who wants to destroy the Earth.

4
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Steven Universe (voice), played by Zach Callison.

5
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Pearl / Yellow Pearl (voice), played by Deedee Magno.

6
00:24:54,000 --> 00:25:00,000
Garnet (voice), played by Estelle.

7
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:09,000
Amethyst (voice), played by Michaela Dietz.

8
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Spinel (voice), played by Sarah Stiles.

9
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:27,000
Greg Universe (voice), played by Tom Scharpling.

10
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Steven Universe: The Movie is a 2019 American animated musical science fantasy television film and a sequel to the
television series of the same name, taking place two years after the series finale "Change Your Mind".

11
00:45:39,000 --> 00:45:45,000
Directed and co-written by series creator Rebecca Sugar with co-direction by Joe Johnston and Kat Morris, the film stars Zach
Callison, Estelle, Michaela Dietz, and Deedee Magno Hall returning from the series, joined by Sarah Stiles.

12
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:54,000
Its plot follows the Crystal Gems as they attempt to save all organic life on
Earth from a deranged Gem with a history with Steven's mother.

13
00:53:57,000 --> 00:54:03,000
The film was announced at San Diego Comic-Con 2018, and a short teaser
trailer was later released on Cartoon Network's YouTube channel.

14
00:58:06,000 --> 00:58:12,000
At San Diego Comic-Con 2019, an official trailer was released, along with the
announcement of a making-of documentary bundled with the film's DVD.

15
01:02:15,000 --> 01:02:21,000
The film premiered on Cartoon Network on September
2, 2019, to 1.57 million viewers.

16
01:06:24,000 --> 01:06:30,000
It was the first Cartoon Network original film
since Regular Show: The Movie (2015).

17
01:10:33,000 --> 01:10:39,000
The film was followed by the epilogue limited series
Steven Universe Future (2019–2020).

18
01:14:42,000 --> 01:14:48,000
The film explores themes of musical, memory loss,
abandonment, vengeance, abandonment issues.

19
01:18:51,000 --> 01:18:57,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
